Q: How to get vaadin selecter with Playwright? A: <p>Wel, I've fixed it. For starters by putting the code in a global-setup.ts and exporting this, it is more clean and a bit secured. Not to make this to complicated I didn't manage to &quot;hide&quot; the credentials but as I'm running this locally for now, no harm is done.</p>
<p>The code:</p>
<pre><code>import { Browser, chromium, expect, Page } from &quot;@playwright/test&quot;;

async function globalSetup() {
  // You can perform any global setup tasks here, such as launching a browser instance.
  const browser: Browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false});
  const context = await browser.newContext();
  const page: Page = await context.newPage();

  await page.goto(&quot;https://****servicestest.ad-***.domain/vo***e-re***ts-ui/login&quot;);
  await page.locator(&quot;vaadin-text-field[name='username'] &gt; input&quot;).fill(&quot;LOGINNAME&quot;);
  await page.locator(&quot;vaadin-password-field[name='password'] &gt; input&quot;).fill(&quot;MY_PASSWORD&quot;);
  await page.getByRole(&quot;button&quot;, { name: &quot;Log in&quot; }).click();
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(&quot;https://****servicestest.ad-***.domain/vo***e-re***ts-ui/&quot;);
  // save the state of the webpage - means we are logged in
  await page.context().storageState({ path: &quot;tests/playwright/.auth/user.json&quot; });

}

export default globalSetup;
</code></pre>
<p>I'm working for a company with applications that have a lot of legacy from old times. As we are bringing the company into new applications and methods, Vaadin still needs to be maintained as is. I hope the new applications will be more systematic and consequent. But nevertheless I need to learn to work with this framework</p>
<p>Thanks all for your time,</p>
<p>Cheers!</p>
